---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  DropdownMenuActions,
  DropdownMenuChat,
  DropdownMenuChecks,
  DropdownMenuControlled,
  DropdownMenuMenubar,
  DropdownMenuPlayground,
  DropdownMenuSelection,
  DropdownMenuSidebar,
} from '../../components/DropdownMenuDemo';
---

<Docs title="Dropdown Menu" description="Action menus with checkboxes, radio groups, submenus, and shortcuts.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Dropdown Menu</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A list of actions behind a button. Use it for row and page actions, bulk actions on a narrow toolbar, filters, and
    account menus. Arrow keys move through items, and focus returns to the trigger when it closes.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="dropdown-menu-demo">
    <DropdownMenuPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Dropdown menu usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import {
  DropdownMenu,
  DropdownMenuContent,
  DropdownMenuGroup,
  DropdownMenuItem,
  DropdownMenuSeparator,
  DropdownMenuTrigger,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/dropdown-menu";

<DropdownMenu>
  <DropdownMenuTrigger
    render={<Button variant="ghost" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Actions for row 1042" />}
  >
    <MoreH size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
  </DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <DropdownMenuContent align="end">
    <DropdownMenuGroup>
      <DropdownMenuItem onClick={edit}>Edit row</DropdownMenuItem>
      <DropdownMenuItem onClick={history}>History</DropdownMenuItem>
    </DropdownMenuGroup>
    <DropdownMenuSeparator />
    <DropdownMenuItem variant="destructive" onClick={remove}>
      Delete row
    </DropdownMenuItem>
  </DropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass a <code>Button</code> to <code>DropdownMenuTrigger</code> through <code>render</code>. Icon-only triggers
      need an <code>aria-label</code>. Disable the trigger with <code>disabled</code> on either part, and set{' '}
      <code>aria-busy</code> while work runs.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sizes</h2>
    <p>
      <code>DropdownMenuContent size</code> is <code>"anchor"</code> (the default: as wide as the trigger, at least
      8rem) or <code>"menu"</code> (a fixed 16rem). Use anchor for text triggers like “Selected actions” and short row
      menus. Use menu for icon triggers with icon items, longer labels, and two-line choices. Both stay inside the
      viewport and scroll when tall.
    </p>
    <DropdownMenuActions client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Placement</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>side</code>, <code>align</code>, <code>sideOffset</code>, and <code>alignOffset</code>. Menus open below
      and start-aligned by default. Composers and footers use <code>side="top"</code>. The menu flips when there is no
      room.
    </p>
    <DropdownMenuChat client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">States</h2>
    <p>
      A busy trigger changes its label and sets <code>aria-busy</code>. Items take <code>disabled</code>; they stay
      readable at half opacity and can’t be chosen. When work finishes, show the result next to the trigger and offer
      only the actions that still apply.
    </p>
    <DropdownMenuSelection client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Checkboxes and radios</h2>
    <p>
      <code>DropdownMenuCheckboxItem</code> and <code>DropdownMenuRadioItem</code> show a check on the right. They keep
      the menu open so people can change several options; filters also pass <code>closeOnClick={'{false}'}</code> to say
      so outright. Pass <code>closeOnClick</code> to close after one choice.
    </p>
    <DropdownMenuChecks client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Links and submenus</h2>
    <p>
      Render an item as a link with <code>render={'{<a href="…" />}'}</code> or your router’s link.{' '}
      <code>DropdownMenuSub</code> nests a menu: the <code>DropdownMenuSubTrigger</code> adds a chevron and opens{' '}
      <code>DropdownMenuSubContent</code> to the side. Long names truncate inside the 16rem menu.
    </p>
    <DropdownMenuSidebar client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Controlled</h2>
    <p>
      Control the menu with <code>open</code> and <code>onOpenChange</code> to open it from a shortcut.{' '}
      <code>finalFocus</code> on the content decides where focus lands when it closes.
    </p>
    <DropdownMenuControlled client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Menubar</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Inside Base UI Menubar"
      code={`import { Menubar } from "@base-ui/react/menubar";

<Menubar>
  <DropdownMenu>
    <DropdownMenuTrigger className="menubar-trigger">File</DropdownMenuTrigger>
    <DropdownMenuContent alignOffset={-4} sideOffset={8} className="min-w-48">
      <DropdownMenuItem>New task<DropdownMenuShortcut>⌘ N</DropdownMenuShortcut></DropdownMenuItem>
      <DropdownMenuItem inset>Duplicate</DropdownMenuItem>
    </DropdownMenuContent>
  </DropdownMenu>
</Menubar>`}
    />
    <DropdownMenuMenubar client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="dropdown-menu-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>DropdownMenu</code>, <code>DropdownMenuTrigger</code>, <code>DropdownMenuPortal</code>,{' '}
      <code>DropdownMenuGroup</code>, <code>DropdownMenuSub</code>, <code>DropdownMenuRadioGroup</code>, and{' '}
      <code>DropdownMenuSeparator</code> wrap the Base UI menu parts and take their props, including <code>render</code>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>DropdownMenuContent</code> renders its own portal and positioner. It takes
      <code>size</code>, <code>side</code>, <code>align</code>, <code>sideOffset</code> (4), <code>alignOffset</code>{' '}
      (0), <code>collisionPadding</code> (8), <code>container</code>, and every Base UI popup prop such as{' '}
      <code>finalFocus</code>. <code>DropdownMenuSubContent</code> takes the same props and defaults to{' '}
      <code>side="right"</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>DropdownMenuItem</code> takes <code>variant</code> (<code>"default"</code> or <code>"destructive"</code>)
      and <code>inset</code>. <code>DropdownMenuLabel</code>, <code>DropdownMenuSubTrigger</code>, and the checkbox and
      radio items take <code>inset</code> too. <code>DropdownMenuShortcut</code> is a plain <code>span</code> for hint
      text; it does not bind keys. Every part sets a <code>data-slot</code>, and you can override it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The trigger has <code>aria-haspopup="menu"</code> and <code>aria-expanded</code>. Enter, Space, and Arrow Down
      open the menu. Arrow keys move, typing jumps to a matching item, Arrow Right opens a submenu and Arrow Left closes
      it, and Escape closes the menu and returns focus. Disabled items can still be reached with arrow keys so people
      know they exist, but they can’t be chosen.
    </p>
    <p>
      Menus fade and scale in from the trigger over 120ms. Motion turns off when reduced motion is requested. In
      forced-colors mode the highlighted item gets an outline.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Menus use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-hover</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code>--sprout-danger</code>,{' '}
      <code>--sprout-danger-subtle</code>, <code>--sprout-shadow-overlay</code>, and the panel and control radii. They
      need no brand color, so they look the same with the neutral and TulipFarm themes in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
